The diagram shows the graph $y=f(x)$, which is made up of line segments and a semicircle.

\exfigure{34_q7_1}

What is the value of $\displaystyle\int_0^{12} f(x)\,dx$?

solutions.latex:
\exfigure{339_q5_s1}

The integral is the area between $y=|x-1|$ and the $x$-axis: a triangle for $-2\le x\le 1$ (base $3$, height $3$) and a triangle for $1\le x\le 2$ (base $1$, height $1$).

$$\begin{aligned} \int_{-2}^{2}|x-1|\,dx &= \dfrac{1}{2}\times 3\times 3+\dfrac{1}{2}\times 1\times 1 \\ &= \dfrac{9}{2}+\dfrac{1}{2} \\ &= 5 \end{aligned}$$
